#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# whittaker_m

#% text
# `whittaker_m(k, m, z)` gives the Whittaker function `M_(k, m)(z) = exp(-z/2)*z^(m + 1/2)*hypergeometric_1f1(m - k + 1/2, 1 + 2*m, z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 13.14.2; `M` solves Whittaker's equation `w'' + (-1/4 + k/z + (1/4 - m^2)/z^2) w = 0`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
whittaker_m(1, 0.5, 1.0)
#% output
#= 0.6065306597126334

#% cell
whittaker_m(0.5, 0.25, 2.0)
#% output
#= 0.9948565892668342

#% cell
whittaker_m(1.2, 1.5, 3.0)
#% output
#= 4.355464529230369

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The definition through `hypergeometric_1f1`:

#% cell
whittaker_m(0.3, 0.7, 1.2) - exp(-0.6)*1.2^1.2*hypergeometric_1f1(0.9, 2.4, 1.2)
#% output
#= -2.220446049250313e-16

